      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The impact of the TPP on the working class remains a heavily debated topic in political economy. Critics argue it favored corporate interests by promoting free trade that led to job outsourcing and wage stagnation in the US. Conversely, supporters contend that the agreement boosted overall economic growth and created new opportunities through market access. Ultimately, the de facto results were mixed, with uneven distribution of benefits across different sectors and skill levels.",
